//! Every HealthKit data type identifier declared in the iOS 27.1 SDK headers
//! (`HealthKit.framework/Headers/*.h`, Xcode, read on 2026-10-25). The iOS app embeds the
//! same list, asks for read access to all of it and writes `catalog.json`; `healthaccess
//! doctor` and `get_catalog` compare the catalog against this list so that a type with
//! data that is not exported, or a type Health knows that this build does not, is
//! reported on every check (`docs/export-coverage.md`).
//!
//! Generated by grep over the headers (`HK_EXTERN <Family>TypeIdentifier const <Name>`);
//! regenerate the same way when a new SDK ships. Deprecated identifiers are kept because
//! Health still holds their samples.

/// SDK the list was read from.
pub const SDK: &str = "iOS 27.1";

